// This extension point can be used to provide custom logic for resolving the actual type of a SoftLink in Java or 
// OpenAPI. It is particularly useful in scenarios where a single custom SoftLink type is not sufficient and additional 
// resolution logic is required.

// Note: 
//		If you just need one custom soft link type then you can also configure that simply inside the Maven 
//		configuration of JEAF Generator using params `javaGenericSoftLinkType` and `openAPIGenericSoftLinkType`.

// Target Output: Java
// since: #3
// Description:
//		Function returns the Java type that should be used for a specific soft link property. How the type is evaluated
//		is decided by the provided custom implementation.
//
String getDynamicSoftLinkTypeForJava(JMM::SoftLink softLink):
	"java.lang.Double";


// Target Output: OpenAPI
// since: #3
// Description:
//		Function returns the OpenAPI type that should be used for a specific soft link property. How the type is 
//		evaluated is decided by the provided custom implementation.
//
String getDynamicSoftLinkTypeForOpenAPI(JMM::SoftLink softLink):
	"integer";
	